From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: use dmabuf inode ID for GRALLOC-backed output blocks

In byte-buffer mode, VideoFramePool::getBufferIdFromGraphicBlock() uses the
GRALLOC branch, which expects a legacy C2BufferPoolData of TYPE_BUFFERPOOL.
Blocks fetched from BASIC_GRAPHIC have null pool data (causing a null-pointer
dereference crash), while AIDL bufferpool2 blocks carry a different pool type
and fail with "not bufferpool-backed".

Identify GRALLOC-backed blocks by their dmabuf inode number, matching the
existing BUFFERQUEUE path, so recycled graphic blocks retain stable buffer IDs
regardless of the backing pool implementation.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/components/VideoFramePool.cpp b/components/VideoFramePool.cpp
index ae5cd34..f57f87b 100644
--- a/components/VideoFramePool.cpp
+++ b/components/VideoFramePool.cpp
@@ -35,6 +35,10 @@ std::optional<uint32_t> VideoFramePool::getBufferIdFromGraphicBlock(C2BlockPool&
     ALOGV("%s() blockPool.getAllocatorId() = %u", __func__, blockPool.getAllocatorId());
 
     switch (blockPool.getAllocatorId()) {
+    case C2PlatformAllocatorStore::GRALLOC:
+        // bufferpool2 blocks are not TYPE_BUFFERPOOL and basic pool blocks have no pool data,
+        // so the bufferpool id works for neither. The dmabuf id survives recycling.
+        FALLTHROUGH;
     case V4L2AllocatorId::SECURE_GRAPHIC:
         FALLTHROUGH;
     case C2PlatformAllocatorStore::BUFFERQUEUE: {
@@ -69,8 +73,6 @@ std::optional<uint32_t> VideoFramePool::getBufferIdFromGraphicBlock(C2BlockPool&
             return static_cast<uint32_t>(id);
         }
     }
-    case C2PlatformAllocatorStore::GRALLOC:
-        FALLTHROUGH;
     case V4L2AllocatorId::SECURE_LINEAR: {
         std::shared_ptr<_C2BlockPoolData> blockPoolData =
                 _C2BlockFactory::GetGraphicBlockPoolData(block);
